jpg"},{"id":100954,"name":"Gianni Franco","role":"Dentista","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/wbMI5l9SG5WVLRQExFD4mdq7pWH.jpg"},{"id":2198822,"name":"Felicitè Mbezelè","role":"Donna delle pulizie"},{"id":2702335,"name":"Barbara Gioli","role":"ragazza solarium","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/4A7wUBNAVSuqadyRua6OR186ahV.jpg"}],"crew":[],"videos":[],"watchProviders":[],"episodeGroups":[],"translations":[{"language":"it-IT","title":"Caccia al tesoro","overview":"Domenico Greco è un attore teatrale di “insuccesso”. Naviga nei debiti e vive a sbafo in casa della cognata Rosetta, vedova di suo fratello. Rosetta ha un figlio di nove anni, malato di cuore. L’unico modo per salvarlo da una morte sicura sarebbe operarlo in America. Ma l’operazione costa 160 mila euro. E né Rosetta, né lo zio Domenico li hanno.  Disperati, i due vanno a pregare sotto la statua di San Gennaro. Chiedono un miracolo. Trovare i soldi dell’operazione. E San Gennaro risponde…dando loro via libera per “prendersi” uno dei gioielli della sua Mitra custodita insieme al famoso Tesoro nella cripta della chiesa. In realtà, a dare voce a San Gennaro è il posteggiatore del parcheggio fuori la chiesa che dà via libera agli automobilisti. Le sue parole rimbombano nella navata attraverso una finestra aperta della cupola. E Domenico e Rosetta, sentendole arrivare dall’alto, le scambiano per quelle del Santo Gennaro."},{"language":"en-US","overview":"Domenico Greco is an unlucky stage actor drowning in debt, living as a freeloader in the home of his sister-in-law, Rosetta—the widow of his late brother—who has a nine-year-old son suffering from a heart condition. The only way to save the boy is through surgery in America, but the procedure costs 160,000 euros. In their desperation, they turn to Saint Januarius in prayer, begging for a miracle. The saint seemingly \"responds,\" giving them the green light to \"take\" one of the jewels from his miter—kept alongside his famous treasure in the church crypt. In reality, it is merely the voice of a parking attendant echoing through the nave—a sound that Domenico and Rosetta mistake for a message from Saint Januarius. Joined by Ferdinando, Cesare, and Claudia, they embark on a \"treasure hunt\" that takes them from Naples to Turin, and eventually to Cannes, on the French Riviera."}],"images":{"logos":[],"posters":[],"backdrops":[]},"poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/eiq0tpsU7aXez3nV8pqWG6LdYHt.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/OlANoe5VfUcyCmDna3agpLpeW4.jpg","seasons":[],"schema":{}}},"artworkLibrary":{"tmdb":{"schemaVersion":1,"source":"tmdb","id":468199,"type":"movie","originalLanguage":"it-IT","series":{"poster":{"it":{"status":"available","selected":{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/eiq0tpsU7aXez3nV8pqWG6LdYHt.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/eiq0tpsU7aXez3nV8pqWG6LdYHt.jpg","language":"it","width":800,"height":1200},"candidates":[{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/eiq0tpsU7aXez3nV8pqWG6LdYHt.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/eiq0tpsU7aXez3nV8pqWG6LdYHt.jpg","language":"it","width":800,"height":1200},{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/mE9Sc0hhaOwOUWUFaLCz3picfwo.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/mE9Sc0hhaOwOUWUFaLCz3picfwo.jpg","language":"it","width":1300,"height":1857},{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/fmw39QchlVkWzukdscoQCPQYw1X.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/fmw39QchlVkWzukdscoQCPQYw1X.jpg","language":"it","width":1300,"height":1857},{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/uBVRSmBEWdfAw1zKV2TUmNulNG2.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/uBVRSmBEWdfAw1zKV2TUmNulNG2.jpg","language":"it","width":1014,"height":1440},{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/haR2i9uajoqgHgNniNEv8hStQz1.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/haR2i9uajoqg